From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dennis Cheng <dennis.cheng@discordapp.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 21:56:22 +0000
Subject: fix: recover from RenderProcessHost reuse race instead of
 CHECK-crashing the browser process
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Avoid CHECK-crashing the browser process when a renderer process host is
re-initialized from inside a render-process-gone handler (e.g.
webContents.reload() called synchronously on renderer crash, as the Discord
client does).

Chromium 148 (crrev.com/c/7031539) added a launch-time CHECK in
RendererStartupHelper::OnRenderProcessLaunched asserting the process was
registered at OnRenderProcessHostCreated. A synchronous reload re-enters
RenderProcessHost::Init() mid-ProcessDied observer iteration: the re-fired
OnRenderProcessHostCreated no-ops because the dead process's map entry is still
present, UntrackProcess then erases it, and the CHECK aborts when the new
process finishes launching.

Upstream already fixed this exact reuse race on Android (crrev.com/c/7330559)
by re-registering the process — restoring the mojom::Renderer remote and
observer without re-running full InitializeProcess (which could re-send
loaded-extension state). This patch extends that recovery to all platforms. The
skipped re-initialization only matters for renderers hosting extension content,
which doesn't apply to Discord's windows.

diff --git a/extensions/browser/renderer_startup_helper.cc b/extensions/browser/renderer_startup_helper.cc
index cacaf4fe5faf634e263546bef9111b8841ec1297..0df1221d8a8d24ccc248c8f465c0a0e25e0ef98a 100644
--- a/extensions/browser/renderer_startup_helper.cc
+++ b/extensions/browser/renderer_startup_helper.cc
@@ -266,8 +266,7 @@ void RendererStartupHelper::OnRenderProcessLaunched(
     // extensions should have already been initialized in
     // OnRenderProcessHostCreated(), if it corresponds to the same context.
     ExtensionsBrowserClient* client = ExtensionsBrowserClient::Get();
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
-    // On Android and ChromeOS, handle race condition during process restart:
+    // Handle race condition during process restart:
     // 1. OnRenderProcessHostCreated() initializes extensions and populates
     // process_mojo_map_.
     // 2. Process startup fails in some cases.
@@ -280,10 +279,6 @@ void RendererStartupHelper::OnRenderProcessLaunched(
         client->IsSameContext(browser_context_, host->GetBrowserContext())) {
       RegisterProcess(host);
     }
-#else
-    CHECK(GetRenderer(host) != nullptr ||
-          !client->IsSameContext(browser_context_, host->GetBrowserContext()));
-#endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
     return;
   }
   // Otherwise, we should *not* have initialized the host yet.
